==Notes==
* {{note|fada|'''a'''}} Vowels with an acute accent are read as [á/é/í/ó/ú] {{lang|ga|fada}} "long [á/é/í/ó/ú]".
* {{note|-th-|'''b'''}} In the verbal adjective suffix, -{{vr|th}}- becomes {{vr|t}} after {{vr|d, gh, l, n, s, t, th}} ({{vr|gh, th}} are deleted before it is added) and it becomes {{vr|f}} after {{vr|bh, mh}} which are deleted before it is added.
* {{note|/h/|'''c'''}} After consonants, {{IPA|/h/}} is silent, but devoices preceding voiced consonants. See [[Irish phonology#Devoicing|Irish phonology]].

